#
# Semantic content of the header page: values, relations and properties.
# The presence of each name and type comes with the Tier 0 generator.

assertion  XBD.stdarg.h.001
anchor     basedefs/stdarg.h.html#DESCRIPTION/va_arg
class      required
says       va_start() and successive va_arg() calls return the arguments in
           order, whatever their types (int, double, long, long long, pointers, a
           structure).
test       t/001-va-arg-sequence.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdarg.h.002
anchor     basedefs/stdarg.h.html#DESCRIPTION/va_copy
class      required
says       va_copy() makes a second list in the same state as the first: reading
           it gives the arguments the original would give next, and reading one
           list does not move the other.
test       t/002-va-copy.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdarg.h.003
anchor     basedefs/stdarg.h.html#DESCRIPTION/va_start
class      required
says       A va_list can be passed to another function that reads arguments with
           va_arg(), and then be ended; a variadic function can be traversed more
           than once, each traversal bracketed by va_start() and va_end().
test       t/003-va-list-passing.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdarg.h.004
anchor     basedefs/stdarg.h.html#DESCRIPTION/va_arg
class      required
says       va_arg() may read an argument as the signed or unsigned type matching
           its own when the value fits both, and a void pointer as a pointer to a
           character type or the reverse.
test       t/004-va-arg-compatible-types.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdarg.h.005
anchor     basedefs/stdarg.h.html#DESCRIPTION/va_arg
class      conditional
when       XSI
says       On an XSI system va_arg() may read a pointer argument as a pointer of
           any other type, and the pointer converted back is the original.
test       t/005-va-arg-pointers-xsi.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdarg.h.006
anchor     basedefs/stdarg.h.html#DESCRIPTION/va_arg
class      required
since      1988
says       A variable argument read with va_arg as the corresponding
           signed or unsigned type gives the same value when it is
           representable in both, and a void pointer and a character
           pointer read as each other give the same pointer.
note       Only the exceptions to the compatibility rule that the page
           lists are used, with small positive values.
test       t/006-va-arg-compatible.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
